{"answer": "It is denied by default. A tool with no row in the authority table (`apps/api/src/oversight/toolAuthority.ts`) is treated as `requires_human_action` and never executes. `authorityOf` only matches the table's own keys, so an inherited property name such as `toString` is denied too. A blocked call does not throw. It returns a normal result, `{\"error\":\"requires_human_action\",\"escalation\":\"blocked_consequential_call\"}`, and a human handles the request in the TMS. The same default applies at both enforcement points. In addition, `assertAllToolsDeclared.ts` makes the api refuse to start if the live tool registry contains a name the table doesn't cover.", "sources": ["specs/support-agent-human-oversight/spec.md (FR-003, FR-004)", "issue-33", "pull-280", "docs/human-oversight.md", "apps/api/test/toolAuthority.test.ts"]}
```

